Subtask 3.9: Understanding Grafana Architecture
Based on your exploration, Grafana's architecture consists of:

Frontend: Web-based user interface for creating dashboards and visualizations
Backend: Server that processes queries and serves the web interface
Data Sources: External systems that provide data (databases, APIs, etc.)
Dashboards: Collections of panels that display visualizations
Panels: Individual visualization components within dashboards
Plugins: Extensions that add new data sources, visualizations, or apps
